From a9e1c1796bab58da3a688f51e73d6cf228843f05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devarsh Thakkar <devarsht@ti.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2025 20:56:18 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] TI: drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: Remove duplicate code for phy
 cleanup

This removes duplicate phy related cleanup code which was causing
duplicate calls to phy_power_off and phy_exit functions thus
causing the phy->power_count to -1 and hence breaking the resume
cycle after system suspend as shown in below logs :

Debug Logs:
"79.515845: phy_power_off: Entered : phy_power_off at 394 power_count = 1
79.515848: cdns_dphy_power_off: Entered : cdns_dphy_power_off at 433
79.515971: phy_power_off: Entered : phy_power_off at 411 power_count = 0
79.515974: phy_power_off: Entered : phy_power_off at 394 power_count = 0
79.515976: phy_power_off: Entered : phy_power_off at 411 power_count = -1"

Failure logs:
[   79.653630] ti-sci 44043000.system-controller: ti_sci: wakeup
               source:0x10, pin:0xff, mode:0x0
[   79.671285] am65-cpsw-nuss 8000000.ethernet: set new flow-id-base 19
[   79.688310] am65-cpsw-nuss 8000000.ethernet eth0: PHY
[8000f00.mdio:00] driver [TI DP83867] (irq=POLL)
[   79.688344] am65-cpsw-nuss 8000000.ethernet eth0: configuring for
phy/rgmii-rxid link mode
[   79.701966] am65-cpsw-nuss 8000000.ethernet eth1: PHY
[8000f00.mdio:01] driver [TI DP83867] (irq=POLL)
[   79.701983] am65-cpsw-nuss 8000000.ethernet eth1: configuring for
phy/rgmii-rxid link mode
[   80.320814] cdns-dsi 30500000.dsi: Timed Out: DSI-DPhy Clock and Data
Lanes not ready.
[   80.820932] cdns-dsi 30500000.dsi: Timed Out: DSI-DPhy Clock and Data
Lanes not ready.
[   82.172670] tc358762 30500000.dsi.0: error initializing bridge (-110)

Fixes: 750442b99e0a ("drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: Fix phy de-init and flag it so")
Signed-off-by: Devarsh Thakkar <devarsht@ti.com>
(cherry picked from commit 28fe7134779cecd2660ffc80c9fcbd863994ae34)

[ECU-1270: from ti-linux-6.12.y, newer than the TI base af3896fca24b.
 With the duplicated block the D-PHY power_on op is skipped after the
 first display disable. Since cip11 0672 (upstream cdns-dphy change,
 PLL programmed in power_on) the D-PHY PLL then stays at the first
 mode's rate when the display mode changes; seen on the ECU-1270 board
 2026-11-16 (WIZ_PLL_CTRL stays 0x811E0202, the 1080p rate, for
 1280x720 and 640x480). Same patch-id as TI's commit.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c
index c657b5da41662..8683e206637fc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-core.c
@@ -627,11 +627,6 @@ static void cdns_dsi_bridge_atomic_post_disable(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	phy_power_off(dsi->dphy);
 	phy_exit(dsi->dphy);
 
-	dsi->phy_initialized = false;
-	dsi->link_initialized = false;
-	phy_power_off(dsi->dphy);
-	phy_exit(dsi->dphy);
-
 	pm_runtime_put(dsi->base.dev);
 }
 
